comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-01T08:25:57.892Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: all-status searches for the exact CodeQL rule, append path, and polynomial ReDoS found closed alerts pm-v3zd3o and pm-8og4 in distinct path/link parsers, but no item for alert 33 or SDK append trailing whitespace. GitHub source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/security/code-scanning/33"
  "2026-08-01T08:33:09.621Z","harness:codex","Evidence: replaced the unbounded trailing-whitespace regex with String.prototype.trimEnd(), preserving the exact append body result. The existing spacer/provenance test now feeds 100,000 repeated spaces as a defect-reproducing negative control. Linked suite passed 20/20; repository coverage passed 411 files and 6,653 tests at exact 100% statements (46,874/46,874), branches (33,722/33,722), functions (9,544/9,544), and lines (45,505/45,505). ESLint, zero-clone, 100% docstring/static quality, SDK boundary/parity/token/calibration/surface/import-cost/transport gates, and secret scan pass. Hosted CodeQL on the PR is the required alert-closure gate."
